derivations.claim:
Since $F=dA$ with $A\in C^2$, its homogeneous identity is $
abla_aF_{bc}+
abla_bF_{ca}+
abla_cF_{ab}=0$. Contraction with $F^{ac}$ gives $2F^{ac}
abla_aF_{bc}=	frac12\partial_b(F_{cd}F^{cd})$. The product rule in the explicit Maxwell tensor therefore yields $$
abla_a(T^{\mathrm{EM}})^a{}_b=\mu_0^{-1}\left[(
abla_aF^{ac})F_{bc}+F^{ac}
abla_aF_{bc}- rac14\partial_b(F_{cd}F^{cd})ight]=\mu_0^{-1}F_{ba}
abla_cF^{ca}.$$ These are continuous identities for $F\in C^1$. If the sourced Maxwell equation holds, the last expression is $-F_{ba}j^a$, which cancels the scalar force term in step 4.2 when $E_\varphi=0$. This proves total-stress conservation and current conservation before any Einstein equation. No smooth-only stress or Noether theorem is invoked at the classical regularity.
